WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.340
Gandalf.

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:04.290
What is the background of this strange wanderer?

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.240
Where did he come from, and why is he meddling
in everyone's affairs?

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:12.280
Let's dive into Gandalf’s backstory and
see what sets him up for the critical role

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.920
he ends up playing throughout The Hobbit and
Lord of the Rings.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.440
Gandalf comes into existence at the beginning
of time.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:25.260
He is a supernatural entity, created by author
Tolkien's supreme being, Ilúvatar.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:31.380
Ilúvatar himself moves into Arda, Tolkien’s
name for the world his stories take place

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.320
within, and he's joined by a host of other
celestial beings like himself, called Ainur.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.600
All of this takes place thousands upon thousands
of years before The Lord of the Rings.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.880
During his "youth", Gandalf is named Olórin.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.980
He lives in the lands to the west of Middle-earth.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.879
He spends a good deal of his time in Lorien,
a heavenly land filled with gardens, lakes,

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:54.380
and rivers.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:00.360
He also keeps company with Nienna, a Valar,
or leader, of the Ainur who is known for her

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.640
association with grief and sorrow.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:09.100
Gandalf is drawn to the "Children of Ilúvatar",
the Elves and Men in Tolkien’s world, and

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:09.980
is always keen to help them.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:16.120
However, he typically doesn't reveal himself
to them in his true form, instead choosing

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:22.040
to communicate to them through visions, hence
the name Olórin, which is translated as "fantasy"

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.920
or "dream" in these stories.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.380
The supernatural Ainur are the highest order
of beings in Middle-earth.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.560
They're broken into two different groups:
The Valar and the Maiar.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:40.060
The Valar, made up of 14 Ainur including Nienna,
are the kings and queens that rule over creation

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.340
in the name of Ilúvatar.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.980
The rest of the Ainur are a group called the
Maiar.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.980
In the book Unfinished Tales, Tolkien refers
to these creatures as an "angelic" order.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:55.660
It's not known how many Maiar there are, but
several of them show up throughout Middle-earth

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:56.160
history.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.560
Sauron, for instance, is probably the most
well-known Maiar.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.000
The Balrog is another, less powerful example.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.900
However, while these two are forces for evil,
there were many other Maiar that fight for

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.340
good, including Gandalf.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:15.860
While he isn't as impressive on the surface,
the Grey Wanderer's great claim to fame is

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:21.540
that in The Silmarillion he's referred to
as "the wisest of the Maiar", an impressive

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.840
trait in a group of mighty immortal spirits.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.820
As well as being the wisest of the Maiar,
Gandalf is also a wizard.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:34.880
"I am Gandalf, and 'Gandalf' means me."

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.560
The "wizard" title is a bit of a misnomer
when compared to the modern English definition

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.160
of the word.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.240
In Unfinished Tales, Tolkien explains the
difference.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.480
Tolkien's "wizard" is a translation of the
Elvish word "istar", representing an order

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.040
that has "eminent knowledge of the history
and nature of the World."

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.420
These wizards, or "Istari", are distinct from
the sorcerers and magic peddlers typically

00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.700
associated with the name.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.960
In reality, they're semi-divine beings.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:09.019
There are five main wizards in Tolkien's writings,
referred to in The Two Towers as, quite simply,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:09.820
the "Five Wizards".

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.859
However, Unfinished Tales explains that their
total number is unknown, and that some may

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.100
have visited regions beyond the northwestern
portion of Middle-earth.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.620
The Istari are technically angelic, supernatural
beings from the glorious west.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:29.580
However, a Maiar becomes a wizard when they've
voluntarily been wrapped in a frail mortal

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.080
body.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:34.540
And this isn't just putting on an appearance
so that they can blend in with Men and Elves,

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:35.040
either.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.440
Their bodies age and die, just like the bodies
of humans.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:44.079
It's made clear in Unfinished Tales that the
physical forms that the wizards take restrict

00:03:44.079 --> 00:03:48.999
their abilities and result in, quote, "dimming
their wisdom and knowledge and confusing them

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.439
with fears, cares, and wearinesses coming
from the flesh."

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.640
This restriction is a natural side effect
of the wizards' purpose in life.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:01.800
The wizards were created and sent to Middle-earth
specifically to help resist Sauron.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.680
Because of this, The Silmarillion says that
they were forbidden to simply overpower the

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:12.300
Dark Lord with godlike powers, nor were they
allowed to dominate Men or Elves when in battle.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:16.720
While he's been around from the beginning
of Time, it turns out that it isn't until

00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:21.340
well into the Third Age that Gandalf is asked
to take on his wizardly form.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:26.780
In Unfinished Tales, the head of the Valar,
Manwë, chooses Gandalf to become the, quote,

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.280
"director and coordinator of attack and defense."

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.479
However, Gandalf resists the nomination, as
he is afraid of Sauron's power.

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:39.830
But Manwë insists, explaining that his wise
caution is precisely why he is perfect for

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:40.380
the job.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:45.760
The five main wizards are chosen and begin
to arrive on the western coast of Middle-earth,

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.380
approximately one millennium into Middle-earth’s
Third Age.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:55.500
This roughly coincides with the time Sauron
begins to set himself up in Mirkwood, as the

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.020
Necromancer we eventually meet in The Hobbit
trilogy.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:05.020
According to one version of the story, Gandalf
is the last Istari to arrive, and it's said

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.080
that he's very unimpressive.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:11.620
He's shorter than the others, already has
grey hair, and leans on a staff.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.420
In fact, the text says that he appears to
be, quote, "least" of the now-mortal Maiar.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:21.080
Of the Five Wizards, Gandalf is obviously
the most well known to readers.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:25.120
Two others appear at times throughout The
Hobbit and Lord of the Rings stories, but

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.700
the last two have no active part in the narrative.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.360
Each of these five representatives of the
Valar has different strengths, but they weren't

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.840
meant to function as a team.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:37.020
The most impressive of the Five Wizards is
Saruman.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.699
Known as "the Man of Skill", he is the first
to arrive in Middle-earth.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.820
He dresses in white, which contrasts boldly
with his hair, which is raven black, at first.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.760
Next up, we have Radagast.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.400
Clad in earthen brown, Radagast is interested
in beasts and birds.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.000
Last and certainly least, as far as the story
goes, are the Blue Wizards.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.860
This pair of Maiar, dressed in sea-blue clothing,
are named Alatar and Pallando, and it's said

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.180
that they traveled to Middle-earth as friends.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.880
While having five elite wizards wandering
around Middle-earth sounds like a great way

00:06:20.889 --> 00:06:25.780
to fight back against Sauron, it turns out
that the only member of the team that genuinely

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.020
has a net positive effect is Gandalf.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:33.340
Tolkien refers to him as the only one who
remains "faithful" to his mission of providing

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:34.580
aid to the free folk.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.780
Saruman's failure is well documented.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:42.400
The Wizard becomes corrupt with power and
goes against the Istari by dominating others

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.120
and actually trying to replace Sauron.

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:51.120
Radagast's fate is quietly tragic, as the
wizard slowly slips into an obsession for

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:55.580
birds and beasts rather than Elves and Men,
fading into obscurity.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:07:00.160
The Blue Wizards are fascinating to hardcore
Tolkien fans because almost nothing is known

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:00.660
about them.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:05.180
Tolkien talked about them as if they were
a riddle that he didn't have time to solve.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:10.360
It's said that the duo traveled far into the
east with Saruman but never came back.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:15.960
In 1958, Tolkien explained they may have founded
faraway cults after failing their mission.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:22.620
When Gandalf first meets the shipwright Círdan,
the Elven lord immediately sees right through

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:27.099
the wizard's lowly appearance and recognizes
the important role that Gandalf is going to

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:28.820
play in the war against Sauron.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:34.120
This leads Círdan to give Gandalf a ring
of power to help him throughout his adventures.

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:38.990
No, not the "One Ring" of power, but a powerful
piece of enchanted jewelry nonetheless.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:44.629
Círdan's gift is Narya the Red, one of the
three Elven rings.

00:07:44.629 --> 00:07:49.360
The ring is meant to help support Gandalf
through his labors and spark courage in others.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.480
While Gandalf accepts the gift, he attempts
to keep it secret.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:57.520
However, he's unable to conceal it from Saruman,
who becomes jealous over the preferential

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.020
treatment.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:02.860
In fact, according to Tolkien, this is the
event that begins to erode the friendship

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:04.060
between the two wizards.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:08.759
When the Five Wizards arrive in Middle-earth,
the events of The Hobbit and The Lord of the

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.600
Rings are still roughly 2,000 years in the
future.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.640
So what does Gandalf do to kill the time?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.500
Turns out, we don't know.

00:08:15.509 --> 00:08:19.479
His name rarely appears in the history of
this lengthy period, and he seems to have

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.880
fallen off the map for huge chunks of time.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:27.520
Fortunately, Tolkien gives us a little hint
in Unfinished Tales when he says,

00:08:27.539 --> 00:08:33.849
"Probably he wandered long (in various guises),
engaged not in deeds and events but in exploring

00:08:33.849 --> 00:08:39.540
the hearts of Elves and Men who had been and
might still be expected to be opposed to Sauron."

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:44.959
In other words, he spends a lot of time wandering
all over the Westlands of Middle-earth, generally

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:49.600
laying low, making friends, and increasing
his understanding of the lay of the land.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:54.290
He doesn't settle down at all during this
point, either, remember, he's known as the

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:56.620
"Grey Wanderer" or the "Grey Pilgrim".

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:01.740
With so many centuries of wandering under
his belt, it's natural that Gandalf would

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:02.900
acquire many nicknames.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:08.280
The name Gandalf means "the Elf of the Wand",
since Men thought he was an Elf.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:12.120
Tolkien himself admitted that he got that
one directly out of Norse mythology.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:17.060
Beyond that, the Wandering Wizard reveals
in The Two Towers that, quote, "many are my

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:18.620
names in many countries".

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:23.200
We've already heard of Olórin, his name in
the West at the beginning of Time.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:28.029
The Elves also call him Mithrandir, which
means "the Grey Pilgrim."

00:09:28.029 --> 00:09:33.780
Adding to the list of monikers, the Dwarves
call him Tharkûn, which translates to "Staff-man."

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:37.280
He also says that in the South he's called
Incánus.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:42.060
However, Tolkien himself seemed to be unsure
about how to explain this last one.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:47.700
In one note, he says that it comes from the
Haradrim language and meant "alien" or "North-spy."

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:52.760
However, in later notes, he claimed it was
just a common name for the Grey Pilgrim in

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:57.580
One other important activity that Gandalf
participates in prior to The Lord of the Rings

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.040
is befriending Hobbits.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:04.820
Gandalf is the only wizard who sees the value
of the Halflings, making a distinct effort

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:08.680
to cultivate a deep connection with the agricultural
community of the Shire.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:13.440
He also entertains the Shire-folk whenever
possible, establishing a reputation for his

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:16.820
incredible fireworks, magic tricks, and excellent
storytelling.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:21.110
On the flip side, he also gets a bit of a
bad rap throughout their tranquil community

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:26.100
for convincing many quiet Hobbit "lads and
lasses" to run "off into the Blue for mad

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:27.100
adventures."

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:32.600
A thousand years after Gandalf’s arrival,
he visits the fortress of Dol Guldur in southern

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:35.810
Mirkwood, where Sauron has been rebuilding
his power.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:41.450
The wizard drives the Dark Lord out, leading
to the centuries-long period called the Watchful

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:41.940
Peace.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:47.300
Galdalf also serves as a member of the Council
of the Wise, or the White Council.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:51.480
It's composed of Saruman, Galadriel, and Elrond,
among others.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:57.600
Gandalf actually leads this prestigious body
at one point, but later leaves, and the position

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:00.880
is awarded to his fellow wizard Saruman instead.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.520
At one point, Gandalf searches for the missing
Dwarven king Thráin II.

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:10.000
In his search, he journeys through Moria and
then revisits Dol Guldur.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:15.339
Here, he finds a Dwarf, who gives him a map
and a key for the Lonely Mountain.

00:11:15.339 --> 00:11:21.270
He also finally discovers that the Necromancer
has returned, and is just Sauron in disguise.

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:25.610
He urges the White Council to attack while
their enemy is unprepared.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:30.360
The Council eventually attacks and defeats
Sauron, at which point Gandalf withdraws to

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:31.020
Mordor.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:35.820
As we get into the events of The Hobbit, Gandalf’s
backstory is drawing to a close.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:40.980
At this point, we find Gandalf in Unfinished
Tales, riding to the Shire for a sabbatical.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:46.820
As he nears the inn called the Prancing Pony,
he ponders the impending evil threats scattered

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:47.980
throughout Middle-earth.

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.600
Suddenly, he encounters Thorin Oakenshield.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:56.720
The Dwarven hero is also deep in thought as
he travels in exile thanks to Smaug the dragon,

00:11:56.730 --> 00:12:00.510
who has taken up residence in his mountain
home half a world away.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:04.540
The two begin to talk, and Gandalf decides
to visit the dwarf's new home.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:08.480
After further discussion, the wizard heads
to the Shire to contemplate.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:14.020
Not long afterward he hears about the eccentric
Hobbit Bilbo Baggins, whom he hasn't seen

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.580
since Baggins was a child.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:19.380
He starts making a plan, and the rest is Middle-earth
history.

